# React conventions

- Use **functional components** and hooks.
- Prefer `const Component = () => { ... }` and `export default Component` (match existing files).
- Keep event handlers named `handleX` and state setters named `setX`.

## State & effects

- Keep `useEffect` focused; if it grows, extract helper functions.
- When reading/writing to `localStorage`, guard for `typeof window === "undefined"` where relevant (match `Navbar.jsx`).

## Markup & accessibility

- Use semantic HTML (`button`, `nav`, `main`) and include `type="button"` on buttons.
- If an element is interactive, ensure it has an accessible label (`aria-label` / `title`) where needed.
